/-! ## Thread `Inputs.memoryWalkAlpha` from fibre `alphaM`

Chip `memoryWalkAlpha` is the memory-walk recurrence challenge `αm`.  Compute and memory each get a
`RAP_walk` gadget; JointCoins is `((αc, γ), (αm, z))`.  On the honest
fibre, `honestCoin` pins `alphaM` to `E.cfg.challenges.α`, and
`honestZeroFamily` already writes that same coordinate into the chip
family.  `atJointCoins` at `honestCoin` therefore sets
`memoryWalkAlpha = alphaM`.  Sibling overlay `inputsOfFibreAlphaM` threads the field.  `packageOf`'s signature is
unchanged.  Fibre `Accepts` stays `∀ a g`. -/

/-- Overlay fibre memory-walk α onto a named `Inputs` record.
Same object as `honestZeroFamily.memoryWalkAlpha` and as `atJointCoins`
at `honestCoin`.  Independent of later-round `(a, g)` -/
def inputsOfFibreAlphaM {E : BuildableNockExecution F K} (I : Inputs E) :
    Inputs E :=
  { I with memoryWalkAlpha := E.cfg.challenges.α }

